      "blocks": [
        {
          "heading": null,
          "bullets": [
            "The majority of candidates were able to give two advantages for using recombinant human factor VIII, instead of factor VIII from donated blood. The most popular reasons given related to medical considerations such as reduced risk of disease transmission or fewer problems with immune responses. A number of candidates described valid ethical considerations.",
            "Some responses were too vague, simply noting that recombinant factor VIII could be produced in large quantities or was easily available."
          ]
        }
      ]
